From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:18:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 101/101] docs(design): report the reaper read-transport result
 at the shipped budget

The first write-up measured forced budgets (3s/2s), which showed the mechanism
but not the everyday case. Twelve interleaved samples of each script at the
SHIPPED 8s budget, same contention, same 12 candidates: 6 of 12 complete scans
before, 11 of 12 after. That reproduces this bead's own 63%-of-cycles-unfinished
tally on demand, and the remaining 1 in 12 is the stated bound showing up rather
than a surprise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md | 37 +++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md b/docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md
index ab06b64..82e892b 100644
--- a/docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md
+++ b/docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md
@@ -329,20 +329,41 @@ transports agree on it. The check that could not be run, ran.
 
 ### Effect, measured on gascity-packs (12 candidates, dry-run, scratch log)
 
+**At the SHIPPED 8s budget**, twelve samples of each script interleaved so both
+saw the same contention (host load ~30-36, 16 cores). The outcome is the last
+terminal event of the cycle:
+
+    complete scans    pre-change  6 of 12       post-change  11 of 12
+
+That ratio is the bead, live. §1's tally from the reap log — 88
+`budget_exhausted` against 51 `scan_complete`, 63% of cycles not finishing — is
+the same number seen from the other end, and the pre-change 6/12 reproduces it
+on demand.
+
+A single interleaved pair, showing where the pre-change cycle dies:
+
+| | pre-change | post-change |
+|---|---|---|
+| candidates examined | 7 of 12 | **12 of 12** |
+| terminal event | `worktree_budget_truncated`, reason `budget_spent_before_git_status`, then `budget_exhausted` | `scan_complete` |
+
+That reason code is one of §4's 17 `budget_spent_before_git_status` lines: the
+budget was gone before a millisecond-scale local `git status` could run on
+candidate 8. Decisions agree wherever both scripts reach the same candidate.
+
+Forced-budget controls, same rig:
+
 | budget | pre-change | post-change |
 |---|---|---|
-| 8s | `scan_complete` 12/12, 4s remaining | `scan_complete` 12/12, **5s** remaining |
 | 3s | `budget_exhausted` — **1 of 12**, deferred 11 | **`scan_complete` 12/12** |
 | 2s | `budget_exhausted` — 1 of 12 | `budget_exhausted` — 1 of 12 |
 
